INT. NOVALOOP STARTUP OFFICE - NIGHT

An open-plan office, lit only by monitors. Beanbags. A whiteboard covered in arrows. Takeaway boxes on every desk.

THE TEAM (six developers) sits in a row of desks, headphones on, typing in perfect sync.

KIM sits at a corner desk, laptop open, hood up. KIP, in a cardigan, approaches slowly with two mugs.

Kip sets one mug down. Kim doesn't look up.

KIP
I made you tea.

KIM
Thanks.

Kip waits. Kim keeps typing. THE TEAM keeps typing.

KIP
You've been on that file for an hour.

KIM
Just tidying up.

Kip glances at the screen. Looks away. Looks back.

ON SCREEN: a file labelled CLIENTS_Q3.xlsx, uploading to an external server. 67%.

ON PHONE: (Kim's phone, face-up) you have 10 min. don't be late.

KIP
That isn't tidying.

KIM
It's a backup.

KIP
To who?

Kim stops typing. Slowly closes the laptop halfway. Looks up.

KIM
Kip.

KIP
Kim. I'm not stupid. I wrote half that database.

KIM
I know.

THE TEAM stops typing. All six heads turn at once.

KIP
They've got us on a deadline, and now you're sending the clients off the books.

KIM
It's a lot of money. More than I'll ever make here.

KIP
It's stealing.

KIM
It's leverage.

The upload bar pings. 100%.

Kip steps back. THE TEAM stands as one. Nobody speaks. A printer somewhere clicks.

KIM (CONT'D)
(softly)
Please sit down. Please.

KIP
No.

They turn and walk toward the exit. Kim stands.

KIM
Kip!

Kip keeps walking. The door opens. Kip stops in the frame.

ON PHONE: (Kip's, buzzing) call me when ur out. we need to talk about kim.

Kip turns back, phone in hand, and holds it up. Kim reads it. Goes pale.

KIM (CONT'D)
That wasn't meant for you.

KIP
I know. That's why it's so good.
